# Deny everything, then name what the build needs. Stated this way round, a new
# file at the repository root — a credential, a local override, an editor's
# scratch state — cannot reach the build context by default, and a `COPY .` can
# never pick up more than the list below.
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE.txt
!infrahub_sync
!opsmill_prefect_extras

# Build outputs of the two allowed trees; nothing here belongs in an image.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
